WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:03.880
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:19.260
The presence of great role
models, which honestly I

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:21.600
think like combined
with the fact

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.590
that MIT'S arts programs
are available to everyone,

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:28.410
and not just people who
have a sheet of paper that

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:30.840
says they're in an arts major.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.780
Those two things like
really helped me personally,

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:37.030
and I think a lot
of other people too.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:40.390
My experience of getting
off doing improv,

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:46.910
I mean like improvising when I
sing jazz is just like, I think

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:49.880
the first step is you
just have to get over,

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:52.790
you have to get over yourself.

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:55.430
Improvisation is a good
part of any theater.

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.490
The highest risk improvisation
is during performances

00:00:58.490 --> 00:00:59.970
when someone doesn't
have something

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:03.560
they're supposed to have,
or one light turns pink.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:06.100
That was a really fun one.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.040
I think it's really
important to create

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.380
spaces that welcome failure.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:13.020
Because for me, like when
I first jumped into art,

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.480
like I was making things
I had never made before.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.190
And obviously as an
artist, as you grow,

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:19.440
you're definitely going to
look back on your past work

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:23.610
and be like wow that
is honestly awful.

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:25.830
And Infinite and definitely
this organization, that's

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:27.247
what's happening
and that's what's

00:01:27.247 --> 00:01:29.580
allowing people to
grow and continue

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:33.180
to allow new people to come
in so that when we leave,

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.400
there are people who
have grown and outgrown

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:38.360
and can continue leading.

